# JS Code Quality (classic ASPX)

Defers to `00-core-fsm` (anti-overengineering / anti-sycophancy) and `14-security-appsec`.
Do **not** apply `01-react-standards` or React/Next MUST rules to this tree.

## Mindsets
- Simplicity · readability · maintainability over premature micro-opts
- Less code = less debt
- **Minimal diffs** — touch only the task; no drive-by cleanup

## Naming
- `camelCase` functions/vars; `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` module constants
- Units in names (`timeoutMs`); collections plural; booleans as questions
- Event handlers `handle*`
- No leftover `d`, `tmp`, `obj`, `x`, or vague `data` when the domain name is known

## Guidelines
- Early returns over deep nesting
- Small pure helpers over sprawling functions
- DRY only when duplication is real and stable
- Handle rejected promises (`await` / `.catch` / intentional `void` + why)
- Check `res.ok` on `fetch`

## Globals (ASPX-safe)
- Prefer IIFE / one namespaced object over ad-hoc `window.*`
- **NEVER** stash secrets on `window`; leave SharePoint host globals unless the task requires them

## Comments
- WHY only. Workarounds: reason + date

## Reject
- New libraries without approval
- Converting classic controller JS into React/SPFx in the classic tree
- `eval` / unsafe `innerHTML` with user data (`14-security-appsec`)
